    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Task dispatch: sync vs async match",
      "description": "How tasks reach a worker. A sync match is handed straight to a poller that was already waiting; an async match had to be written to the backlog and picked up later. A queue running almost entirely on async match is a queue that is never caught up -- measured here at 0.9/s sync against 84/s async on the workflow side while the backlog stood at ~10k.",
